    "question": "A book has 8 chapters. Beth has read 2 chapters in 3 hours. If she continues reading at that rate, in how many hours will she be able to finish reading the remaining chapters?",
    "gold": "9",
    "answer": "Beth still needs to read 8 - 2 = <<8-2=6>>6 chapters.\nShe can read 1 chapter in 3/2 = <<1.5=1.5>>1.5 hours.\nTherefore, she will be able to finish reading the remaining chapters in 1.5 x 6 = <<1.5*6=9>>9 hours.\n#### 9"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many hours it will take Beth to finish reading the remaining chapters, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the reading rate:**\n   Beth has read 2 chapters in 3 hours. Therefore, her reading rate is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Reading rate} = \\frac{2 \\text{ chapters}}{3 \\text{ hours}} = \\frac{2}{3} \\text{ chapters per hour}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the number of chapters remaining:**\n   The book has 8 chapters in total. Since Beth has already read 2 chapters, the number of chapters remaining is:\n   \\[\n   8 \\text{ chapters} - 2 \\text{ chapters} = 6 \\text{ chapters}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the time required to read the remaining chapters:**\n   Using the reading rate, we can find the time required to read the remaining 6 chapters:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Time} = \\frac{6 \\text{ chapters}}{\\frac{2}{3} \\text{ chapters per hour}} = 6 \\text{ chapters} \\times \\frac{3}{2} \\text{ hours per chapter} = 9 \\text{ hours}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of hours it will take Beth to finish reading the remaining chapters is \\(\\boxed{9}\\).",
